-- Facts restated in Boston Daily's own words with attribution. Every story carries its own photo; none was used in an earlier package or open draft (grepped content/ and seed/).
-- loc.gov and Wikimedia Commons could not be opened from the newsroom sandbox on this run. Photo URLs are Wikimedia Commons thumbnails built from file names confirmed by search (MD5 path). Four are U.S. government works (White House, Senate, House, Navy); four carry a Commons free license that the editor should confirm. The image check falls back to 800px or the original file if a thumbnail size is missing.
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO stories (id, slug, lane, type, section_slug, status, sensitive, headline, dek, body, byline, hero_image_url, hero_image_credit, hero_image_rights, source_system, source_ref, priority, is_lead_candidate, created_by, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('bd-20261119-trump-xi-putin-trilateral', 'trump-xi-putin-first-three-way-meeting-shenzhen-no-agreements-announced', 'newsroom', 'news_story', 'white-house', 'EDITORIAL_REVIEW', 0, 'Trump, Xi and Putin hold the first three-way meeting of U.S., Chinese and Russian leaders in Shenzhen, with no agreements announced', 'The talks on Thursday, Nov. 19, Shenzhen time, ran about an hour and 20 minutes and followed a separate Trump-Putin meeting. Zelenskyy said U.S. envoys would brief Ukraine and European leaders in Berlin.', 'President Trump, Chinese President Xi Jinping and Russian President Vladimir Putin met at a villa in Shenzhen, China, on Thursday, Nov. 19, local time, on the sidelines of the Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation summit. The session lasted about an hour and 20 minutes and was chaired by Xi, according to Ukrainian outlet UNN, citing Reuters and Chinese state media. No results had been announced when it ended.

## What the leaders said

Opening the session, Trump called it the first-ever meeting of the three countries'' leaders and said it was an honor to be in the room with both men, Russia''s TASS news agency reported. He said the group was making history, according to UNN. Putin said the three countries share many interests in settling regional conflicts, including the war in Ukraine. Xi did not mention Ukraine and spoke instead about whether great powers would live in harmony or clash.

Reuters analysts quoted by UNN did not expect significant agreements, citing deep differences over Ukraine, Iran, nuclear weapons and trade.

## The Putin meeting first

Before the three-way talks, Trump met Putin on his own. Trump said that meeting "set the stage" for the session with Xi and that "something will come out" of the summit, ABC News reported. He has said he wants to discuss limits on nuclear weapons, Iran and an end to the war in Ukraine. The trade truce between Washington and Beijing that ended the 2025 tariff fight expires on Jan. 10, 2027, CBS News reported.

## Ukraine and Europe wait for a briefing

In his nightly address, Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy said he expects U.S. envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner to brief him on the talks in Berlin on Thursday, Nov. 19, Euronews reported. Germany, France and Britain are co-hosting that meeting, and more than 30 European leaders are expected. Zelenskyy said decisions about Ukraine must be made with Ukraine at the table.', 'Boston Daily Staff', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/P20250815DT-0225_President_Donald_Trump_meets_with_Russian_President_Vladimir_Putin_at_Joint_Base_Elmendorf_Richardson_in_Anchorage,_Alaska.jpg/1280px-P20250815DT-0225_President_Donald_Trump_meets_with_Russian_President_Vladimir_Putin_at_Joint_Base_Elmendorf_Richardson_in_Anchorage,_Alaska.jpg', 'President Trump meets Russian President Vladimir Putin at Joint Base Elmendorf-Richardson in Anchorage, Alaska, on Aug. 15, 2025 (file). Official White House photo via Wikimedia Commons, public domain', 'public_domain', 'newsroom', 'content/2026-11-19.sql', 9, 1, 'newsroom-assistant', '2026-11-19T10:55:00.000Z', '2026-11-19T10:55:00.000Z');
